<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83919" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλίσσομαι</span></b> , aor. 1
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπλιξάμην </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Ach.</u>
			218
		</span></i>: pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπλιγμαι </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δια-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Archil.
			58
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cross the
				legs,</i> as in <i>trotting,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ μὲν τρώχων, εὖ δὲ πλίσσοντο
				πόδεσσιν</span> well they galloped, well they <i>trotted,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.318
			</span></i>:—
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα πλίσσωσιν
			ὁμαρτῇ</span> cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				243
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλίξαντα: διαναβάντα καὶ
				ἀναστάντα καὶ διαβάντα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλήξ</span>-cod.).</div>
